title: Agricultural Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
on-arrival: agricultural_policy_timer += 6; month_actions += 1; agricultural_policy_timer += 6
view-if: sect_agriculture_party = "R" and agricultural_policy_timer = 0
card-image: img/portraits/Julian.jpg
tags: potus_affairs, cabinet

= Agricultural Policy

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> Party must address the crisis of Southern agriculture. Former plantations lie fallow, freedmen demand land, and poor whites face ruin. Our Northern industrial base wants cheap cotton and food, while Southern <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republicans**</span> people need economic survival. <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> push for confiscating Confederate estates, while <span style="color: #9D2933;">**Moderates**</span> prefer market solutions.  

- @land_reform
- @land_reform2
- @agricultural_finance
- @pro_consumer
- @state_buyer
- @root: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@land_reform
title: 40 Acres and a Mule
subtitle: -1 budget - Break up Confederate plantations for freedmen’s homesteads.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget <= 0 : Requires 1 budget. ?] [? if judicial_reform < 2 : The courts wouldn't support such action ?]
choose-if: judicial_reform >= 2 and budget > 0
view-if: fifth_A = 0
on-arrival: {!
    Q.budget -= 1;
    Q.PoliticalCostPenalty += 1;
    Q.freemen_rep += 3;
    Q.land_reform += 1;
    Q.rural_dem -= 5 * (1 - Q.dissent);
    Q.radical_strength += 6;
    Q.moderate_dissent += 4;
    Q.kkk_militancy += 0.1;
    Q.liberal_strength += 3;
    Q.liberal_dissent -= 2;
    Q.Forty_Acres += 1;

    // Delivering a core Radical demand satisfies Radical-leaning voters
    // with the regular party, undercutting the breakaway party's appeal
    // even as its leadership is pleased.
    if (Q.radical_split == 1) {
        Q.freemen_rad -= 2;
        Q.rural_rad -= 1;
    }
    if (Q.liberal_split == 1) {
        Q.rural_lib -= 1;
    }
!}

We seize rebel estates under the Confiscation Acts, granting land to freedmen’s cooperatives. Former slaves become yeoman farmers but ex-Confederates scream of ‘Negro domination.’ The Klan burns crops in response.

@land_reform2
title: 40 Acres and a Mule
subtitle: Break up Confederate plantations for freedmen’s homesteads without compensation
unavailable-subtitle: [? if judicial_reform < 2 : The courts wouldn't support such action ?]
choose-if: judicial_reform >= 2
view-if: fifth_A = 1
on-arrival: {!
    Q.freemen_rep += 4;
    Q.land_reform += 2;
    Q.rural_dem -= 6 * (1 - Q.dissent);
    Q.radical_strength += 7;
    Q.moderate_dissent += 5;
    Q.kkk_militancy += 0.2;
    Q.agriculture_goal_completed += 1;
    Q.liberal_strength += 4;
    Q.liberal_dissent -= 3;
    Q.Forty_Acres += 1;

    if (Q.radical_split == 1) {
        Q.freemen_rad -= 3;
        Q.rural_rad -= 2;
    }
    if (Q.liberal_split == 1) {
        Q.rural_lib -= 2;
        Q.middle_class_lib -= 1;
    }
!}

The Reconstruction government has authorized a bold land redistribution effort: seizing and subdividing former Confederate plantations for freedmen, without compensating their former owners. Thanks to judicial reform and a revised Fifth Amendment, the courts now allow such a radical move.

@agricultural_finance
title: Freedmen’s Credit
subtitle: -2 budget - Increase financing for agricultural credit and insurance.
choose-if: budget >= 2
on-arrival: {!
    Q.budget -= 2;
    Q.PoliticalCostPenalty += 2;
    Q.agricultural_finance += 1;
    Q.rural_rep += 6 * (1 - Q.dissent);
    Q.rural_dem -= 4;
    Q.kkk_strength -= 5;
    Q.rural_policy += 1;
    Q.economic_growth += 0.2;
    Q.moderate_strength += 2;
    Q.liberal_strength += 1;
    Q.conservative_dissent += 1;

    // A moderate, market-based tool: it doesn't satisfy the Radicals'
    // core demand, so it does little to pull their voters back.
    if (Q.liberal_split == 1) {
        Q.rural_lib += 2;
        Q.middle_class_lib += 1;
    }
!}

The Freedmen’s Bank expands loans for Black cotton growers and white tenant farmers. Northern investors grumble about risk, but Southern <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> hail it as salvation from sharecropping bondage.

@pro_consumer
title: Bread Subsidies
subtitle: -1 budget – Cheap grain for Northern factories.
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: {!
    Q.budget -= 1;
    Q.PoliticalCostPenalty += 1;
    Q.workers_rep += 5 * (1 - Q.dissent);
    Q.unemployed_rep += 4;
    Q.rural_dem += 3;
    Q.economic_growth += 0.2;
    Q.moderate_strength += 2;
    Q.conservative_dissent += 1;
    Q.dem_reform_strength += 2;

    // Not a Reconstruction-enforcement policy at all, so it neither
    // satisfies nor angers Radical-leaning voters specifically.
    if (Q.liberal_split == 1) {
        Q.workers_lib -= 1;
    }
!}

We flood Northern markets with cheap Midwestern grain. Textile workers cheer, but Southern planters accuse us of ‘starving the South’ to feed Yankee mills.

@state_buyer
title: Cotton Bureau
subtitle: -2 budget – Federal price guarantees for cotton.
choose-if: budget >= 2
on-arrival: {!
    Q.budget -= 2;
    Q.PoliticalCostPenalty += 2;
    Q.rural_rep += 7 * (1 - Q.dissent);
    Q.economic_growth += 0.4;
    Q.uk_relation -= 2.5;
    Q.moderate_strength += 3;
    Q.conservative_dissent += 2;
    Q.liberal_dissent += 1;

    // Helps freedmen farmers directly, so it pulls a little support
    // back from the Radicals just as the land reform options do.
    if (Q.radical_split == 1) {
        Q.freemen_rad -= 1;
    }
    if (Q.liberal_split == 1) {
        Q.rural_lib -= 2;
    }
!}
max-visits: 1

The U.S. Cotton Bureau sets fixed prices, shielding freedmen from exploitative traders. London textile magnates threaten to buy Egyptian cotton instead, while Wall Street howls about needing limited government intervention.